From e584174c13ac6825c9675a3a8b767d00102f1c8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Emilio=20Cobos=20=C3=81lvarez?= <emilio@crisal.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:39:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] comp: Prevent recursive layout computation with template
 unions.

More minimal version of #3419 which avoids the crash even though it
doesn't get the right layout (we'd need to enforce rust unions for
these).

In llvm/llvm-project#185449, LLVM's libc++ changed a header to use a
recursive self-referential type, which looks approximately like:

```
template <class A0, class... As> union RUnion { A0 arg; RUnion<As...> u; };
template <class A> union RUnion<A> { A arg; };
struct Wrap { RUnion<int, float> u; };
```

Uninstantiated union templates don't have a meaningful layout anyway, so
return `None` from `CompInfo::layout` for them.

Closes #3397
